this is Devonte Chisholm reading for  Mark Delaney if you haven't heard by now  the Farm Sim genre that gave us Classics  like Animal Crossing and stardew Valley  is getting a new entry soon Disney Dream  like Valley is in large part exactly  what it sounds like a house of mouse  spin on the popular genre where  characters such as Isabelle and Tom Nook  are replaced by Princess Jasmine and  Scrooge McDuck however Disney dreamlike  Valley is more than just Animal Crossing  dressed in Mickey Mouse ears so we're  breaking down ways in which this new  entry to the genre puts its own spin on  things  perhaps the most important difference  between the two games is that Disney  Dream like Valley is a free-to-play game  when it comes to PC switch Xbox and  Playstation platforms this September  there won't be a price barrier between  fans and the new Disney Experience  Gameloft also made sure to ease tensions  for players who might expect the  typically mobile-centric team to use  more Mobile gaming tactics such as  paying to speed up in-game timers or  buying resources for cooking or building  none of that will be in this game  instead it will feature optional paid  Cosmetics like clothing which will be  available alongside free options too I  also expect some sort of season pass  structure with a premium path that will  reward more Disney themed goodies to  players who buy into it though we're  still waiting to hear more about that  Disney Dream Life Valley is to a great  extent a casual life Sim that lets you  fill your in-game days with whatever you  want to focus on in that time however  there's a whole other section that  involves more story driven levels and  character interactions that don't really  have an equal in Animal Crossing with  dreamlike Valley's Realms you're  transported to various Disney Worlds  such as Remy the rats restaurant from  Ratatouille moana's sunny beaches and  Wally's post eco-apocalyptic planet in  each realm you will complete missions  for the heroes and villains native to  that story land complete their missions  and you'll be able to recruit them to  your neighborhood where they'll  instantly become your new neighbor it's  an interesting Twist on the new neighbor  element of Animal Crossing and Gameloft  said new Realms will be added to the  game often and for free  you start the game with a few neighbors  like Mickey Mouse and Goofy and over  time you see the town filled with new  faces one exciting wrinkle to this very  animal crossing-like aspect is that each  Neighbor comes with their own reward  tree the more you hang out with your  neighbors complete their missions or  give them gifts such as homemade food or  clothing the more they'll appreciate  your companionship you can see previews  of the items you'll get from each of  them each time you level up and with 10  levels for each character in The build I  saw there was a lot worth chasing not  only do you get a hefty Bounty of coin  rewards for spending at Scrooge mcduck's  store but you also get Cosmetics themed  around each character the game seems  full of rewards to keep players invested  and just as long as they keep the Toy  Story Cosmetics coming I'm definitely  invested  let's be honest Animal Crossing didn't  really get the post launch support that  you might have expected from one of the  biggest games in the world in 2020.  Disney Dream like Valley isn't out yet  so it could go a different way but right  now at least game loss intentions seem  to include supporting the game closely  and often it makes perfect sense given  the free-to-play nature of it in  addition to Free Realms and new Disney  properties debuting in the game  regularly the team said players can  expect expansions big and small surely  this means things like new Cosmetics at  the very least but can we expect Star  Wars and Marvel to move into the valley  sometime in the future according to the  dev I spoke to they aren't ruling it out  though there aren't currently any signs  of terraforming like in New Horizons  Disney dreamlike Valley does build on  Nintendo's giant Town customization  options in a major way like Animal  Crossing you can move your home in  Disney dreamlike Valley but what's  interesting here is you can do that  whenever you like for no money at all  want more of a beachfront property just  drag and drop your house to the shore in  the game's build mode as Remy come to  town but you'd prefer his house to be  next to yours rather than scars just  swap them the feature isn't limited to  just you and your belongings every fence  potted plant signpost home and more can  be moved Wherever Whenever you like this  should give players new and old to the  genre quite a thrill as it really opens  up the customization options for  decorating the town precisely to your  heart's desire the same can be said  about clothing if you don't like a piece  of clothing you can customize it with an  intricate layering tool that allows you  to add stamps logos and paint your own  fashion sense right into your wardrobe  your starting area in dream life Valley  is roughly the size of the Animal  Crossing town but it gets bigger over  time as you complete missions you'll  unlock new biomes inspired by different  climates like Jungles and deserts as  well as Brands like Frozen and The Lion  King this gives the setting a lot more  visual variety and when combined with  the customization options really allows  you to theme your Valley exactly as  you'd like want to put all The Lion King  characters in the planes to match the  theme you can like the Friendship  rewards and new Realms new biomes are  just another carrot on the stick for  players who want to be rewarded for  playing  in Animal Crossing food has a number of  uses you can sell it ship it to a friend  place it on a shelf or most importantly  you can eat it for Extra Strength when  tackling a heavy task like breaking a  rock or digging up a tree however you  can easily carry out your day-to-day  tasks without ever touching food in  dreamlike Valley eating actually  restores your stamina bar when you're  out working the feels the mines are down  at the pond all day you're liable to get  fatigue eating food fixes that issue  quickly and easily for when you're in  need and if you're worried about having  to manage this system my pre-launch  experience suggests that there's nothing  to worry about not only is it easy to  refill your energy using Basic Foods  like apples that are growing around town  but if you're totally out of food you  can refill your energy by simply heading  into your house for a moment to  immediately replenish your stamina  there's no need to sleep or step away  from the game  so we've already mentioned the game's  two main modes of play the Freedom Farm  Life Sim and the adventure mode that  takes you into new Realms but there's  also a third story line going on all the  time it revolves around what the  characters call the forgetting in Disney  Dream Live Valley the forgetting was an  event that seems to have wiped  everyone's memories and left dangerous  nightthorns scattered across the land as  the protagonist you show up after it's  taken place and part of your purpose is  to get to the bottom of what it was and  why it occurred while your first order  of business may be obsessively clearing  the night Thorns from each patch of  grass as you find them they represent a  deeper mystery the biomes I mentioned as  well as other landmarks around town are  covered in this Sinister darkness and  while you're not exploring Realms  cooking or designing your own outfits  this forgetting will be a long lasting  mystery that you can dive into by  finding memories around the world or by  completing missions to remove its toxic  influence  Disney Dream like Valley launches in  Early Access for free on September 6th  in a rare feat it's not just hitting PC  via steam Early Access it's also landing  on switch Xbox One series X and S PS4  and PS5 all on the same day and optional  Founders pack will be available at  launch and Xbox game pass ultimate  subscribers will get it as one of their  membership perks though its contents  have yet to be revealed I for one can't  wait to pour more hours into this game  but let me know in the comments if  you're excited for it and stick to  Gamespot for the latest on dreamlife  Valley and more  [Music]  foreign  [Music]
 

